don't put a finger in that socket if you want to pass multiple amps through your cleanroom walls, use a one-way diode. it's also handy when branching off a main power line to limit amps in thinner branches and prevent them from overloading and catching fire.

an mv diode will suffice for now, but you can also consider making an hv diode since you will need to run hv machines in the near future, and you won't have to wait for 100% cleanroom efficiency again when upgrading to hv.

