comparing at a distance comparators are wonderfully useful devices, but their need to be directly next to whatever they are comparing is quite limiting. if you could do so remotely that would free you from one major constraint.

remote comparators allow you to do just that. sneak-right-click with a crystalline eye to bind the block you want to watch, and place the eye in a remote comparator to start monitoring the block remotely.

