pushing back the taint so how do you actually destroy tainted land?

these ethereal blooms will remove tainted lands within a small area around themselves, which in turn kills off any fibrous tendrils. they cannot cleanse tainted nodes, nor will they necessarily return tainted biomes back to what they were before, but they will provide a barrier.

the shimmerleaf they are made from have a recipe in an lv assembling machine if you're having a hard time finding them around silverwood trees. there is also a cropsnh version of them. {"0": {"autoconsume": 0, "consume": 0, "groupdetect": 0, "ignorenbt": 1, "index": 0, "partialmatch": 1, "requireonlyoneitem": 0, "requireditems": {"0": {"count": 1, "damage": 4, "oredict": "", "id": "thaumcraft:blockcustomplant", "resolved": {"id": "i:thaumcraft:blockcustomplant:4", "name": "ethereal bloom", "mod": "thaumcraft", "registry": "blockcustomplant", "icon": 12547, "nbt": null, "kind": "item", "unit": "items", "damage": 4, "shard": "5bf21927749d0a2a", "recipes": 1}, "label": "ethereal bloom"}}, "taskid": "bq_standard:retrieval"}} {}

