helium 3 and saltwater on moon the moon is rich in helium 3 because the sun has been embedding it in the upper layer of moon by the solar wind over billions of years.

salt water is also available in smaller quantities. you can get chlorine out of it. you will want plenty of chlorine for processing rutile to get titanium.

