heavy fuel by adding hydrogen to sulfuric heavy fuel in a chemical reactor you can produce heavy fuel, with a burn value of 360,000 eu per cell! aside from this, it's also required for diesel, in mv, which is a better fuel, and it can also be distilled into three very useful fluids: benzene, toluene and phenol.

if you want to use heavy fuel as a power source, you will need semi-fluid generators, unlike light fuel and diesel which use combustion generators.

