lasers solve everything laser hatches are a high-end way of sending lots of amps of power, so much in fact, that it starts at 256a. this goes 1024/4096/16384+ and continues from there. they're also so powerful that only a few machines support them outside of the ever wonderful tectech: lsc, mbf, enf, and pss. remember to paint the laser vacuum pipes, the source hatch, and the target hatch. also, source = output, target = input. laser vacuum pipes do not split or bend. to turn your laser, use an [note]active transformer[/note]. later on, you can use a laser vacuum mirror to bend your laser vacuum pipes; this will not allow splitting.

[note]laser hatches can have their operational amperage adjusted in their gui.[/note]

[warn]be careful with using very high amp hatches as every laser hatch has 1eu/s * max amps passive power loss. for example, a 256a laser source hatch and 256a laser target hatch will both lose 256 eu/s regardless of the amount of power flowing through.[/warn] {"0": {"index": 0, "taskid": "bq_standard:checkbox"}} {}

