early ethylene in lv, cracking fuels is only possible in a chemical reactor, which has a lower efficiency than the oil cracker multiblock that is available at hv. that said, it is still a great source of some fluids, one of which being ethylene, the precursor to polyethylene, the first plastic that can be produced and a required part of progression in the pack. to obtain ethylene from oil, the best way to go is to severely steam-crack refinery gas.

simply put the refinery gas and the steam in a chemical reactor with the correct circuit (check nei) and then distill the cracked refinery gas. it can give a lot of different outputs, so make sure you choose the right one. after doing this, you'll have successfully processed oil, both for power and for byproducts. congratulations!

